{"pack": "m2talk", "voice": "girl", "speaker": {"af_heart": 1.0}, "audio": "m2talk-20261117.mp4", "model": "Kokoro-82M v1.0 (Apache 2.0) via kokoro-onnx (MIT); misaki phonemizer (Apache 2.0)", "gap": 0.45, "clips": {"{name}! You did it, the lighthouse shines again!": [0.0, 2.271], "Marlo's old sea chart shows a big city across the sea. It's Port Lumen!": [2.721, 4.553], "And the Crumb Crew went that way!": [7.724, 1.823], "My new boat, the Sea Sprout, is ready for long trips. But look at the sea: the tide is going out!": [9.997, 5.833], "At low tide, a sand path goes from this old dock to Port Lumen.": [16.28, 4.041], "It's the Tidewalk. Walk it! Juniper is coming too.": [20.771, 3.167], "Port Lumen? Walk the Tidewalk, {name}! It starts at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [24.388, 4.937], "The Sea Sprout is for long trips, far away. Someday!": [29.775, 3.444], "Mo's boat, the Sea Sprout, is finished. It's waiting at the harbor.": [33.669, 3.828], "Wow, {name}! We walked all the way across the sea! Look at this city: canals, bridges, so many houses!": [37.947, 6.068], "This is Port Lumen. The Tidewalk will take us home whenever we like, from this beach.": [44.465, 4.873], "Barney said the crew sold a page at the market here. Let\u2019s find it! Look, people are waiting for us!": [49.789, 6.068], "So many streets! Good thing you know how to read a map.": [56.307, 2.868], "People are waiting on the pier. Market Street is just up the road. The Town Hall is north, past the big canal.": [59.625, 6.921], "The Sea Sprout is resting, {name}.": [66.996, 1.759], "To go home to Lighthouse Island, walk the Tidewalk from the Old Town beach!": [69.205, 4.319], "\"Welcome to Port Lumen, the city of canals!\"": [73.973, 2.612], "\"Water taxis stop at the yellow signs.\"": [77.035, 2.591], "The big clock on the tower has stopped.": [80.076, 2.207], "Its hands point to ten past three: the time the storm hit.": [82.733, 3.572], "A statue of the person who started the city long ago.": [86.755, 3.081], "The plaque is covered in mud from the storm. You can't read it yet.": [90.286, 3.721], "An old stone well in the Old Town square. Coins sparkle at the bottom.": [94.457, 4.233], "People make a wish when they drop one in.": [99.141, 2.228], "A water taxi stop.": [101.819, 1.567], "Welcome to Port Lumen! I'm Mayor Bea.": [103.835, 2.484], "Since the storm, our big clock has stopped. Nobody knows what time it is!": [106.769, 4.468], "The water taxis are late, the market opens whenever it wants\u2026 what a mess!": [111.687, 4.617], "And someone came to the market selling old pages with maps on them. Very strange!": [116.755, 4.937], "And this is Gus, our clockmaker. He came to meet you!": [122.142, 3.081], "Tick\u2026 tock\u2026 no, nothing. Hello there! I'm Gus, the clockmaker.": [125.673, 3.572], "The night of the storm, my tower shook and some gears slipped. The hands are stuck at ten past three.": [129.695, 5.599], "Help the people of Port Lumen and learn all you can!": [135.744, 2.932], "Take this road to Market Street. Start at Ms. Reyes\u2019s book stall. Go stall by stall to Rafi\u2019s fish market.": [139.126, 6.623], "Then come to my Clock Tower!": [146.199, 1.844], "Huge gears, as big as wagon wheels. They're stuck.": [148.493, 3.252], "Some gears slipped out of place. Gus will need help putting them back.": [152.195, 3.828], "A model of an old sailing ship.": [156.473, 2.036], "A card says it brought the first families to Port Lumen long ago.": [158.959, 3.551], "An empty display case. The card says: \"An old map of the sea\".": [162.959, 4.084], "The map is gone!": [167.493, 1.225], "Today's flavors: vanilla, strawberry, chocolate, mint, mango and blueberry.": [169.169, 4.831], "The ships board: when each boat comes and goes.": [174.449, 2.911], "Every time says \"???\" \u2014 the clock tower stopped, so nobody knows the time!": [177.81, 4.404], "A big map of Port Lumen on the wall.": [182.664, 2.164], "Three canals cross the city. They are the Grand Canal, the North Canal and the Harbor Canal.": [185.278, 5.492], "Old photos of the city long ago. The Town Hall looks almost the same!": [191.22, 4.255], "But there were no water taxis back then: people rowed little boats.": [195.925, 3.849], "Fresh fish! Fresh fish! Hello, I'm Rafi.": [200.224, 2.911], "The storm brought lots of seaweed into the harbor. The fish love it!": [203.585, 3.849], "Hello! I'm Ms. Patel. I teach violin.": [207.884, 2.825], "Every evening I play by my window. Since the clock stopped, I never know when to start!": [211.159, 5.193], "Hi there. I'm Mr. Diaz. I grow vegetables on my roof!": [216.803, 3.721], "The storm blew my tomatoes all over the Old Town. Ha!": [220.974, 3.7], "Hey! I'm Ruby! Want to see me skate? Watch\u2026 whoa!": [225.124, 3.167], "Those pirates ran past me yesterday. One of them was a little bird with a blue feather!": [228.741, 5.257], "Good day, dear. I'm Mrs. Chen. I knit hats and scarves for the whole street.": [234.448, 4.596], "When it gets cold, come and see me.": [239.494, 2.079], "Hi! I'm Leo. I bring the mail on my bike.": [242.023, 2.804], "I ride so fast I'm never late\u2026 but with no clock, I don't know if I'm early!": [245.277, 4.852], "Ah, a new face. I'm Grandpa Walt. Do you play chess?": [250.579, 3.508], "I've lived in the Old Town for seventy years. I remember when the clock was built.": [254.537, 4.553], "Hi! I'm Nora. I run around the park every morning.": [259.54, 3.38], "Did you see the ducks on the pond? They're the best runners\u2026 swimmers!": [263.37, 3.593], "Flowers! Lovely flowers! I'm Mr. Bloom.": [267.413, 2.761], "A flower for every friend. Every friend for a flower!": [270.625, 3.252], "Hi! I'm Hana. I fly kites in the park.": [274.327, 2.825], "From up high, my kite sees the whole city, like a map!": [277.602, 3.231], "Hello, explorer! I'm Officer Dale. I help keep Port Lumen safe.": [281.283, 4.084], "If you see those pirates, tell me. But be careful!": [285.817, 2.868], "A violin and a music stand. The notes say: \"Evening song\".": [289.135, 3.935], "Pots of tomatoes, peppers and beans, ready for the roof garden.": [293.519, 3.871], "A red skateboard covered in stickers.": [297.84, 2.207], "Balls of yarn and two knitting needles. A scarf is almost done.": [300.497, 3.999], "A mail bike with a big basket.": [304.945, 2.015], "A chess board in the middle of a game. Whose turn is it?": [307.41, 3.273], "Running shoes, a little muddy from the park.": [311.133, 2.505], "Buckets of fresh flowers for tomorrow's market.": [314.089, 2.932], "A blue kite with a long red tail.": [317.471, 2.121], "A shiny badge and a whistle on a hook.": [320.042, 2.292], "Hey, I'm Omar. I play guitar on the bridges.": [322.784, 3.231], "The canals make the music sound bigger. Listen!": [326.465, 3.017], "Hi! I'm Lucy, and I build robots!": [329.932, 2.633], "My newest robot can sweep the street. Well\u2026 almost. It mostly spins in circles.": [333.015, 5.492], "Hello, mijo! I'm Mrs. Rivera. I bake cookies for the whole street.": [338.957, 4.255], "Without the clock, I never know when they're ready. I just follow my nose!": [343.662, 4.084], "Smile! Click! I'm Mr. Novak, the photographer.": [348.196, 3.295], "I take a photo of the Town Hall every year. One day, my photos will go in the museum!": [351.941, 5.385], "Hi! I'm Tia! I'm the best goalie on my team!": [357.776, 2.975], "Want to play? Oh, you're on a mission. Okay, next time!": [361.201, 3.273], "Oh, hello, dear. I'm Granny Fern. I've read every book in the City Library!": [364.924, 4.767], "Well, almost every book. The library opened again after the repairs. I go every day!": [370.141, 5.577], "Hi! I'm Kenji. I take care of my fish, Bubbles and Squirt.": [376.168, 3.743], "I come to the canal to look at the wild fish. They're faster than mine!": [380.361, 3.999], "Hi, I'm Zoe! I paint the city from the roofs.": [384.809, 2.953], "Yesterday I painted three pirates running down Market Street. Strange, right?": [388.213, 4.724], "A guitar with colorful stickers. One string is new.": [393.387, 3.252], "A little robot with a broom for an arm. It beeps!": [397.089, 3.124], "A plate of warm cookies. They smell like cinnamon!": [400.663, 2.996], "An old camera and a box of photos of the Town Hall.": [404.109, 3.103], "A shiny trophy and a ball.": [407.661, 1.801], "A tall pile of library books, all read twice.": [409.913, 2.911], "A fishbowl with two orange fish: Bubbles and Squirt.": [413.273, 3.231], "A painting of the canals at sunset. The paint is still wet!": [416.954, 3.7], "Welcome to Sip & Snack! I'm Kiki!": [421.104, 2.42], "The storm broke the Galleria's glass roof. The workers fixed it yesterday, so we're open again!": [423.974, 5.791], "Oh, but there's a problem. My berry smoothies need fresh mint, and I don't have any left.": [430.215, 5.343], "Olive grows mint in the greenhouse, in City Park. Could you ask her for some, {name}?": [436.007, 4.511], "Meanwhile, take a look at what I have!": [440.968, 2.185], "Olive's greenhouse is in City Park, by the pond. She has the best mint in town!": [443.603, 5.065], "Want something while you wait?": [449.119, 1.631], "Is that... fresh mint? It smells amazing!": [451.199, 2.911], "Now I can make smoothies again! The first one is for you, {name}.": [454.56, 3.231], "And here are some shells. Thank you, explorer!": [458.241, 2.655], "Hi again, {name}! What would you like?": [461.345, 1.801], "Good day! I am Mr. Fitz, and I make hats.": [463.597, 2.719], "A good hat keeps the sun out of your eyes. And it makes you feel brave!": [466.765, 3.956], "I made every hat in this shop with my own two hands. Have a look!": [471.171, 3.828], "Ah, my favorite customer! Looking for a new hat?": [475.449, 2.825], "Hey hey! Welcome to Funhouse Toys! I'm Pepper!": [478.725, 2.996], "Kites, yo-yos, boats... Toys don't run out. You can play with them again and again!": [482.171, 4.809], "Back for more fun? Let's see!": [487.43, 1.887], "A fountain under the new glass roof. The water sparkles in the sunlight.": [489.767, 4.276], "Some people make a wish here. What would you wish for?": [494.493, 2.847], "THE GALLERIA: Sip & Snack, Topper Hats, Funhouse Toys.": [497.789, 3.657], "At the bottom it says: \"More shops coming soon!\"": [501.897, 2.889], "Welcome to my library, {name}! I\u2019m Ms. Reyes. The books are back on their shelves.": [505.236, 4.468], "We just opened again after the storm. Most of our books are dry, thank goodness.": [510.154, 5.023], "But one book never came back. Dr. Kai, at the aquarium, borrowed it a long time ago.": [515.627, 5.449], "Could you ask him for it, {name}? Books are happiest on their shelves.": [521.526, 3.273], "The aquarium is right next door, on the east side. Dr. Kai is always busy with his fish!": [525.249, 5.492], "My book! You found it!": [531.191, 1.503], "Thank you, {name}. A library is a place where everyone shares, and that means bringing books back.": [533.144, 5.172], "Here are some shells, for a very helpful reader.": [538.766, 2.783], "Every Saturday I read stories on the rug. You're always welcome, {name}.": [541.999, 3.892], "A soft rug with cushions, for story time.": [546.341, 2.719], "A little sign says: \"Quiet voices, big ideas.\"": [549.509, 3.252], "Big old books: \"Records of Port Lumen.\"": [553.211, 2.633], "Some pages are missing. Maybe somebody in town knows where they are...": [556.295, 4.084], "Welcome to the City Aquarium! I'm Dr. Kai. I take care of all the fish here.": [560.829, 4.66], "Every fish in these tanks is a real fish. They all live in the water around us.": [565.939, 4.639], "Go close to a tank and press A. You can read all about the fish inside!": [571.027, 4.191], "Catch one of these fish in the wild! Then it goes in your field journal. Watching here doesn't count!": [575.668, 5.599], "A library book? Oh no... I forgot all about it!": [581.717, 3.167], "It was under my fish food. Please take it back to Ms. Reyes, and tell her I'm sorry.": [585.333, 5.044], "A tank full of water and plants.": [590.827, 1.951], "Oh! A visitor! Welcome to my greenhouse. I'm Olive.": [593.228, 3.124], "The storm broke three glass panes. Now they're fixed, and my plants are warm again.": [596.802, 5.023], "Here, have a fruit cup. Fresh and sweet!": [602.275, 2.463], "Mint for Kiki? Of course! I have plenty.": [605.187, 2.761], "Here you go. Tell her to save me a smoothie!": [608.399, 2.612], "The bees visit my flowers every day. Go look at the bee box, but don't bother them!": [611.461, 4.873], "Olive's tomato plants climb up tall wooden poles. Some tomatoes are already red!": [616.784, 5.3], "Mint for Kiki? Of course! I have plenty. Here you go.": [622.534, 3.38], "And a fruit cup for you, fresh and sweet. Tell Kiki to save me a smoothie!": [626.364, 4.34], "TREASURE! An old pocket watch, half-buried in the sand!": [631.154, 3.209], "Its hands don't move anymore. It looks very, very old.": [634.813, 3.38], "A letter in a bottle, with a little anchor drawn on it.": [638.643, 2.975], "\"Hello! I'm Ana. I sail a small cargo boat between the islands.\"": [642.068, 4.276], "\"When I come to Port Lumen, I listen for the big clock. This time it was quiet. I hope it gets fixed! \u2014 Ana\"": [646.794, 6.601], "Thank you for helping Gus. Now, a mayor has to think about the past, too.": [653.845, 4.532], "Why did our city do the things it did? Let's think like historians!": [658.827, 3.764], "\u00a1Hola! I'm Pedro, captain of the water taxis!": [663.041, 3.124], "Stand by any yellow sign and press A, and I'll take you anywhere. But first, can you read my canal map?": [666.615, 6.303], "Ahoy! I'm Captain Lin, the harbor master. I know every ship that comes and goes.": [673.368, 4.959], "Three pirates sailed in on a leaky old ship. The Leaky Biscuit, it was called!": [678.777, 4.66], "But my harbor isn't only for pirates. Let me show you what moves through it every day.": [683.887, 5.001], "I sell so many fish that I count them in crates and boxes. Want to learn my trick?": [689.338, 4.745], "Hi hi! I\u2019m Coco! I make the best ice cream in Port Lumen!": [694.533, 4.02], "My freezer stopped in the storm and some ice cream melted. Is it ruined forever? Let's find out!": [699.003, 5.855], "Hey, it's you again! I need help with my sales chart before I order new toys.": [705.308, 4.703], "Bars, numbers\u2026 it's like a game! Ready?": [710.461, 2.548], "Ah, you're back! Can you say what a hat is like, with just the right words?": [713.459, 3.679], "A hat maker needs good words for his signs. Let me teach you.": [717.587, 3.721], "My visitors always ask me questions they could answer themselves\u2026 if they knew how to read a fact page!": [721.759, 6.175], "A fact page tells true things that you can check.": [728.383, 2.676], "Let me show you the secret helpers on every page.": [731.509, 2.889], "Would you like to learn another reader\u2019s trick?": [734.849, 2.377], "Some long words are just two small words holding hands!": [737.676, 3.124], "Hello! I\u2019m Dr. Amara. I take care of the old treasures in the City Museum.": [741.25, 4.852], "Something old and important is missing from my museum: an old sea map! The storm? Or\u2026 someone sneaky?": [746.552, 6.644], "To solve mysteries of the past, we need good questions. Let me show you.": [753.646, 4.297], "Want to see how a real scientist finds things out? My plants are perfect for a test!": [758.393, 5.215], "You came from the island? I grew up on a farm, far from any city. Life there is very different!": [764.058, 5.833], "Want to see my favorite inventor's secret? It's all about pieces!": [770.341, 3.956], "I've lived in the Old Town for seventy years. People thought very differently back then! Sit, I'll tell you.": [774.747, 6.196], "Gears, gears, gears\u2026 When everyone in town has helped, we'll make this clock tick again!": [781.393, 4.916], "Port Lumen is lucky to have you, {name}. Keep asking why!": [786.759, 3.103], "Have you heard of the Castle League?": [790.312, 1.801], "Explorers with all ten medals go to a big castle. Five champions wait there!": [792.563, 4.959], "Need a ride? Stand by any yellow taxi sign and press A!": [797.972, 3.551], "Ships in, ships out. Goods, people and news, all day long!": [801.973, 3.743], "My new freezer works! The melted ice cream froze again. Come back for a scoop!": [806.165, 4.852], "Who? What? When? Why? Keep asking, and the past will answer!": [811.467, 3.508], "You helped the city, {name}, and you\u2019re Canal Cup champion! You know the number line and how pieces fit. Go!": [815.425, 5.769], "Let's fix the big clock together. First the gears, then the time!": [821.645, 3.785], "It's working! Listen\u2026 five more minutes to midnight\u2026": [825.88, 3.145], "DONG! DONG! DONG! The bells are ringing again!": [829.475, 2.868], "Wait. Did you hear that? Someone up there shouted: \"MY EARS!\"": [832.793, 3.529], "Nobody should be above the bells. Take the ladder, {name}. I'll be right behind you!": [836.773, 4.255], "The ladder goes up to the old room above the bells. Go on, I'm right behind you!": [841.477, 4.852], "Tick, tock! My clock has never worked better. Thank you, {name}!": [846.779, 3.188], "The gears turn smoothly now. Tick, tock, tick, tock.": [850.417, 3.38], "Shh! Who's there?! Oh, it's YOU. All right, all right, you found us!": [854.247, 4.361], "I'm Captain Rascal Crumb. We hid up here to read the museum's old sea map in secret.": [859.059, 5.172], "It has an X on it. We thought the treasure was in Port Lumen\u2026 but we dug everywhere and found nothing!": [864.681, 5.791], "Hmph. You think you're so clever? BRIOCHE! Our navigator knows every number in this city. Show this explorer!": [870.921, 7.327], "You\u2026 I didn't think I'd see you again.": [878.698, 2.1], "Doesn't matter! The Crumb Crew is my crew now. Let's see what you've got!": [881.248, 3.743], "Why did you leave him in the storm?. We're not scared of you!.": [885.441, 2.953], "No more talking. Round one!": [888.844, 1.951], "Arr\u2026 you really ARE clever.": [891.245, 1.759], "Fine. Here's the museum's map. And that glowing page? We traded it for a bag of cookies. Yum!": [893.453, 5.961], "The X isn't here anyway. Look: it's on an island far to the south. We'll find it first! Come on, crew!": [899.865, 6.239], "(Pip winks at you before flying after the ship.)": [906.553, 2.719], "Oh! Hello again, little explorer! I'm Barney, the cook.": [909.722, 3.167], "Captain says we're on a treasure hunt. I just want a quiet kitchen\u2026": [913.339, 3.913], "Psst! Squawk! It was me! I left the parrot clues all over town.": [917.702, 3.956], "I wanted somebody to find us. The captain isn't bad, just\u2026 a little greedy. Pieces of eight!": [922.108, 5.599], "Three big bells, still shaking after midnight. Hmmm-mmm-mmm\u2026": [928.157, 4.084], "A note in big messy letters: \"See you on the next island, little explorer! \u2014 Captain Crumb\"": [932.691, 5.407], "The old sea map is back in its case. The X is far to the south\u2026": [938.547, 4.105], "The sea map is back where it belongs! Thank you, {name}.": [943.103, 2.783], "Look at that X\u2026 on an island far to the south. I wonder what's there.": [946.335, 3.999], "The big clock is ticking again. Everyone in Port Lumen knows the time now!": [950.784, 4.212], "{name}, you saved Port Lumen! You\u2019ve done so well\u2026 I have something for you.": [955.446, 3.871], "Look at the end of the pier: a little boat, just your size! I fixed her up myself. She\u2019s yours!": [959.767, 5.577], "The X on the old sea map is on Rootwood Island. It's far to the southeast.": [965.794, 4.596], "Sail the Sea Lane and you\u2019ll find it!": [970.84, 2.079], "Steer her just like walking. I\u2019ll follow you in the Sea Sprout.": [973.369, 3.465], "Would you like to learn to read a clock to five minutes? It\u2019s a clockmaker\u2019s favorite skill.": [977.284, 4.937], "Yes, please!. Maybe later.": [982.671, 1.737], "Your boat is tied at the end of the pier, {name}. Sail east along the Sea Lane to Rootwood Island!": [984.859, 5.364], "I'm Ruby! The storm smashed the little dock at this taxi stop. The water taxi can't stop here!": [990.673, 5.812], "Rafi has planks at the fish market. Learn with the people of Market Street first, then come back!": [996.935, 5.748], "You learned with all of Market Street! Now we can rebuild the dock.": [1003.133, 3.785], "Then the water taxi can stop at the Harbor again, and everyone can ride!": [1007.368, 4.148], "First, a quick review. Every right answer gets you one plank. Then you build! Ready?": [1011.966, 5.065], "You have the planks! Stand by the taxi stop and press A to lay each one.": [1017.481, 4.233], "I count my skateboard tricks in tens. Today: 3 tens and 4 ones! Our dock is the best place to practice.": [1022.165, 7.177], "Five planks, and the dock is as good as new! Here comes the water taxi! YOU built it, {name}!": [1029.792, 5.087], "Let's tell Mayor Bea!": [1035.329, 1.503], "The taxi stop's dock is broken. With planks, you could lay a new one along the canal.": [1037.281, 5.151], "A water-taxi stop\u2026 but its little dock is broken. The taxi can't stop here.": [1042.882, 4.959], "Ruby is looking at it, nearby.": [1048.291, 1.951], "Hi! I'm Leo. I bring the mail on my bike\u2026 but with no clock, I never know if I'm late!": [1050.691, 5.513], "Gus says the storm knocked gears loose in the Clock Tower. Learn with the Canal Walk people first!": [1056.655, 5.812], "You learned with the whole Canal Walk! Gus found five loose gears in the tower.": [1062.917, 4.553], "They go back between the clock face and the big wheels. Gus needs our help!": [1067.92, 4.233], "A quick review first. Every right answer gets you one gear. Then you put them back! Ready?": [1072.603, 5.236], "You have the gears! Go into the Clock Tower. Press A by the big wheels to put each one back.": [1078.289, 5.215], "Five gears, all back in place. Now I just need the bells to tell me the time!": [1083.954, 4.703], "All five gears back in place! You have good hands, {name}.": [1089.107, 2.975], "Now let's turn the big wheel and\u2026 hmm. Wait a moment.": [1092.531, 3.017], "The big wheels of the clock. The five loose gears go back between them and the clock face.": [1095.999, 5.065], "The gears are back in place. But the clock still needs its Bell Gear.": [1101.514, 3.849], "{name}! Listen\u2026 footsteps, ABOVE the bells! And someone said \"shh!\"": [1105.813, 3.956], "Nobody should be up there. I put my old ladder up to the trapdoor. Go and see who it is!": [1110.219, 5.044], "The Bell Gear! Brioche gave it back. Let me put it in\u2026 there!": [1115.713, 3.465], "Tick, tock, tick, tock\u2026 the big clock is working again!": [1119.629, 3.359], "DONG! DONG! DONG! The midnight bells ring all over Port Lumen!": [1123.437, 4.084], "Oh, a visitor! I'm Mei's grandma. Mei's out in the city, but I'm always here with my yarn.": [1127.971, 5.492], "Every winter I knit one hat for each child on our street. I made one too many this year\u2026": [1133.913, 5.151], "It's yours! Keep your ears warm on the boat.": [1139.514, 2.612], "(You got the Wool Beanie! Wear it from your backpack.)": [1142.576, 2.655], "Knit one, purl one\u2026 Counting stitches is good math practice, you know!": [1145.681, 4.319], "I'm Max! Hana's at the park with her kite. I'm watching the bees from our window.": [1150.449, 4.681], "Did you know? Bumble bees can see ultraviolet light. That's a color people can't see!": [1155.581, 5.108], "So flowers look different to a bee! Here, have my shells. Look for bumble bees by day, in the park flowers!": [1161.139, 6.559], "(You got 10 shells!)": [1168.147, 1.46], "Bzzz! I want to be a bee scientist when I grow up.": [1170.057, 3.743], "Hi! I'm Omar's sister, Layla. He plays guitar all day\u2026 I fish the canals!": [1174.25, 4.873], "Want a secret? The largemouth bass hides in the calm canal water, by plants and logs.": [1179.573, 5.556], "It's most active at dawn and dusk. So fish when the sun is low!": [1185.579, 3.871], "And look at its mouth: the jaw reaches back past its eye. That's how it got its name!": [1189.9, 5.044], "(Tip: the largemouth bass bites in the city canals at dawn and dusk.)": [1195.394, 4.041], "Dawn and dusk, remember! That's bass time.": [1199.885, 2.633], "Welcome! I'm Kenji's dad. I fish in the harbor every morning.": [1202.969, 3.956], "Out at sea, Atlantic herring swim together in big schools. One female can lay 30,000 to 200,000 eggs!": [1207.375, 9.908], "That's a LOT of little fish. Here, take my spare hat. Every fisher needs one!": [1217.733, 5.215], "(You got the Yellow Bucket Hat! Wear it from your backpack.)": [1223.397, 3.103], "Kenji named his fish Bubbles and Squirt. He says Bubbles is the boss of the house!": [1226.95, 4.873], "{name}! Did you see that glow in the sea, by the lighthouse?": [1232.273, 2.676], "Go and see it first, by the rocks! Then come back, and we can talk about a trip.": [1235.399, 4.639], "Hello, mijo! Are you the explorer with the Atlas? Then I have something for you.": [1240.488, 4.788], "A raccoon in a big hat gave me this glowing paper\u2026 for a big bag of my cookies!": [1245.726, 4.98], "It hums when you come near. I think it wants to go home. Here, it's yours!": [1251.156, 4.233], "Is the page happy in its book now? Here, have a look at my cookies, mijo!": [1255.839, 4.511], "{name}! You built that dock all by yourself. You are doing so well!": [1260.8, 3.38], "Our trip is long. There are many places to see, and lots and lots of walking.": [1264.63, 4.788], "So I brought you a present. Close your eyes\u2026 Open them!": [1269.868, 3.188], "Juniper rolls out a red bike with a big basket. Your otter jumps right into it and waves!": [1273.506, 5.663], "It's yours! Open your backpack and tap Ride. When you go into a house, you get off by yourself.": [1279.619, 5.407], "Ring the bell and go, explorer!": [1285.475, 2.036], "Those three pirates bought fish and paid with\u2026 cookie crumbs! One had a green parrot on his shoulder.": [1287.961, 5.556], "You learned so much! Now help me count my crates. Then find Ruby by the broken taxi dock at the Harbor.": [1293.967, 6.431], "Here\u2019s something odd. A book about old sea maps was borrowed last week. The card is signed \"C. Crumb\".": [1300.848, 6.452], "Want to learn more? Go and see Lucy, at her robot stall on Market Street.": [1307.75, 4.575], "My robot recorded sounds at the market this morning: three voices\u2026 and a parrot saying \"Pieces of eight!\"": [1312.775, 6.345], "Want to learn more? Go and see Dr. Amara, at her stall on Market Street.": [1319.57, 4.596], "This morning a raccoon in a big hat had a stall by mine. He sold glowing paper\u2026 and packed up fast!": [1324.616, 6.409], "Want to learn more? Go and see Rafi, at the fish market by the harbor.": [1331.475, 4.084], "The thief left tiny paw prints in the dust of the empty case. Raccoon paws, I think. And a cookie crumb!": [1336.009, 6.345], "Want to learn more? Go and see Mr. Bloom, at his flower stall on Market Street.": [1342.805, 4.66], "Strange thing, amigo! The night the clock stopped, I heard a big CLANK in the Clock Tower. Then silence.": [1347.915, 6.281], "Want to learn more? Go and see Rafi, at his fish stall on the Canal Walk.": [1354.646, 4.361], "One more thing! A pirate, an otter in a navigator\u2019s cap, dropped a big shiny gear. He grabbed it and ran!": [1359.457, 6.452], "Want to learn more? Go and see Ms. Reyes, reading by the canal on the Canal Walk.": [1366.359, 4.831], "A clock book is missing: \"How Clocks Ring\". The card says\u2026 \"C. Crumb\". Again!": [1371.64, 4.937], "Want to learn more? Go and see Lucy, with her robot on the Canal Walk.": [1377.027, 4.319], "A clock is many pieces working together. If ONE gear is missing, it stops. No Bell Gear, no bells\u2026": [1381.796, 6.516], "Want to learn more? Go and see Grandpa Walt, at the west end of the Canal Walk.": [1388.762, 4.617], "When I was a boy, the midnight bells were SO loud. They\u2019d scare anyone hiding near. Did someone stop them?": [1393.829, 6.26], "Great job again! Now help Pedro with taxi riders, then find Leo by the Clock Tower. He needs you!": [1400.539, 6.473], "One more thing\u2026 Last night I heard footsteps above the bells. Nobody goes up there!": [1407.463, 5.044], "Want to learn more? Go and see Coco, by the Clock Tower on Museum Road.": [1412.957, 4.511], "A big fellow bought my warmest hat. He said: \"It\u2019s so windy up by the bells!\" Then he ran off.": [1417.917, 5.812], "Gus heard strange noises up by the bells. Go and see him in the Clock Tower!": [1424.179, 4.639], "Every night some ice cream disappears. And there are sticky footprints going toward the Clock Tower!": [1429.268, 5.449], "Want to learn more? Go and see Captain Lin, on Museum Road.": [1435.167, 3.551], "The Leaky Biscuit is still tied at the east docks. But nobody\u2019s aboard. Where did they go?": [1439.168, 5.428], "Want to learn more? Go and see Dr. Amara, in the Museum.": [1445.046, 3.657], "One more account for you: an old guard\u2019s diary. It says there is a secret room above the clock\u2019s bells!": [1449.153, 6.153], "Want to learn more? Go and see Mr. Fitz, on Museum Road.": [1455.757, 3.508], "Guess what? A green parrot bought a toy telescope. It paid with an old gold coin. A parrot! With money!": [1459.715, 6.495], "Look at my map of the harbor floor. Someone drew an X on it in pencil. What are they looking for?": [1466.659, 5.492], "Someone dug holes in my greenhouse last night! They dropped a torn corner of a map. It says: \"\u2026the X\u2026\"": [1472.601, 6.303], "Oh! I remember now. The pirates sold one page at the market. It had a map of the sea, and a nibbled corner!": [1479.354, 6.601], "A big fellow tried on every hat in my shop. He said: \"Captain Crumb needs a new one!\" Then he ran off.": [1486.405, 6.559], "Did you know? The first big clocks had no minute hand at all. People only needed the hour!": [1493.414, 5.215], "Back again, {name}? Business is booming! Boats bring fish, people buy fish\u2026": [1499.079, 4.127], "Watch how fast I add and take away my boxes!": [1503.655, 3.017], "Hello! I\u2019m Ms. Reyes, the librarian. Today my books came out to the market! Books are full of new words.": [1507.123, 6.388], "Don\u2019t know a word? The words around it are clues. Let me show you!": [1513.961, 3.657], "Hi! I\u2019m Lucy, and I build robots!": [1518.068, 2.633], "Every robot starts with choosing the right materials. Want to help me test some?": [1521.151, 4.553], "Before we fix the big clock, you need to think like a clockmaker.": [1526.155, 3.572], "Clock hands jump around a circle, numbers jump along a line. Let me show you!": [1530.177, 4.852], "Good day! I\u2019m Mr. Fitz, the hat maker. See my signs: \"unhappy hat\", \"rewrap the box\"\u2026 so many tricky words.": [1535.479, 7.049], "Little word starts can change a word\u2019s meaning. Let me teach you two!": [1542.978, 3.828], "I found something in the museum basement: two old stories of the same day!": [1547.256, 4.34], "Each one tells what one person saw. Historians compare them. Shall we look together?": [1552.046, 5.065], "You\u2019re doing so much for our city, {name}! Have you heard of the Canal Cup?": [1557.561, 3.593], "A friendly quiz on numbers and all you learn in our city. Three young players want to play: Ruby, Leo, Zoe.": [1561.605, 6.772], "Beat each one to get a badge: Canal, Bridge, and Bell. The city champion rings the big bells with Gus!": [1568.827, 6.452], "Ruby is waiting right outside, on the Town Hall Plaza. Good luck!": [1575.729, 4.212], "Hi! I\u2019m Ruby. My Canal Cup match is all about hundreds, tens, and ones.": [1580.391, 4.916], "Rafi at the fish market can teach you. Learn it, then come back!": [1585.757, 3.785], "Hi! I\u2019m Ruby. Have you met Mayor Bea? She runs the Canal Cup!": [1589.992, 3.849], "I\u2019m Ruby! I count my skateboard tricks in tens.": [1594.291, 2.996], "Yes, let\u2019s go!. Not now.": [1597.737, 1.78], "Rematch? I\u2019ve been practicing my tens!": [1599.967, 2.377], "Wow, you\u2019re fast! Here, the Canal Badge is yours.": [1602.795, 3.039], "You won the Canal Badge!": [1606.283, 1.588], "Mayor Bea will want to hear the news. Go and see her in the Town Hall!": [1608.321, 3.828], "I\u2019m Leo! My match has adding and taking away with big numbers, and questions about what you learned.": [1612.599, 5.983], "Rafi knows a trick for that. Learn it first \u2014 then I\u2019ll race you!": [1619.032, 3.807], "I\u2019m Leo! I add up my bike rides every day.": [1623.289, 2.911], "Another race? This time I\u2019m ready!": [1626.649, 2.164], "You beat me! Nobody ever beats me at big numbers\u2026 until now!": [1629.263, 3.892], "You won the Bridge Badge!": [1633.605, 1.567], "One more match to go: Zoe will be ready in the next chapter.": [1635.622, 3.487], "I\u2019m Zoe. My match is the hardest one: big numbers, story problems AND questions about everything you learned!": [1639.559, 7.028], "Learn all you can in the city first. Then come and find me!": [1647.037, 3.337], "I\u2019m Zoe. I paint numbers on my pictures\u2026 and I solve story problems for fun.": [1650.824, 5.343], "Last match of the Canal Cup! First to 5 points. Ready?": [1656.617, 3.785], "A rematch? Sure! I love story problems.": [1660.852, 2.953], "You did it! You\u2019re the Canal Cup champion!": [1664.255, 2.356], "You won the Bell Badge! You are the Canal Cup champion!": [1667.061, 3.167], "Now go and see Gus in the Clock Tower. The champion rings the big bells!": [1670.678, 4.596], "QUIZ NIGHT at the Town Hall! The whole city is here.": [1675.724, 2.911], "Big news, {name}! A raccoon in a big hat came to the market this morning\u2026 and sold a glowing page!": [1679.085, 5.492], "With a big cook and a green parrot. It\u2019s them: the Crumb Crew! They sold one page and ran off.": [1685.027, 5.833], "They traded it to Mrs. Rivera, our cookie baker. Her cookie cart is right outside, on the plaza!": [1691.31, 6.068], "A blue feather floats down from the Town Hall roof\u2026": [1697.828, 2.847], "Now we know WHO sells the pages, and our taxi dock is fixed! But why is our clock still stopped?": [1701.125, 5.919], "I found out why the clock still won't run, {name}! All the loose gears are back\u2026 but look:": [1707.493, 4.468], "The Bell Gear isn't loose. It's GONE! Someone took it, so the bells can't ring at midnight.": [1712.411, 5.151], "Somebody wanted the bells quiet\u2026 But who is hiding near those bells? Let's find out!": [1718.012, 4.852], "A big boat came in! Now I have boxes of ten and single fish everywhere.": [1723.314, 4.724], "Will you help me count them? Tens and ones!": [1728.488, 2.505], "All counted! You\u2019re a real fish-market helper, {name}.": [1731.443, 2.783], "Let me show him a trick. I toss a shell in\u2026 and he brings it back!": [1734.676, 3.679], "Amigo! My water taxis are full today. People get on, people get off\u2026": [1738.805, 4.553], "Help me count my riders? Adding and taking away to 100!": [1743.808, 3.849], "\u00a1Perfecto! Every rider counted. Thank you, {name}!": [1748.107, 2.697], "Oof! You know your tens and ones better than any navigator, {name}!": [1751.255, 3.401], "Fine, fine\u2026 here's the Bell Gear. I took it so the bells wouldn't wake us. Gus can have it back!": [1755.106, 5.897], "I\u2019m Brioche, the navigator. I know every canal\u2026 and every number in Port Lumen!": [1761.453, 5.023], "Dr. Kai comes running from the aquarium.": [1766.926, 2.633], "A Lanternhorse! I have waited my whole life to see one!": [1770.009, 3.401], "It\u2019s a magic creature of Otterpage, not a real animal. Real seahorses live in the sea, and they don\u2019t glow.": [1773.861, 6.772], "Lanternhorses like that bridge. On some nights it glows there again. Look for it!": [1781.083, 4.873], "Champion! Before we fix the clock, we must set the right time on it.": [1786.406, 3.871], "Let me show you how to read a clock to five minutes. Then we\u2019ll fix it together!": [1790.727, 4.127], "The Canal Badge! Well done, {name}!": [1795.303, 1.844], "Quiz Night starts when you finish this chapter\u2019s lessons and help Rafi with his fish boxes. Come back then!": [1797.597, 6.431], "\u00a1Hola! I\u2019m Pedro, captain of the water taxis!": [1804.478, 3.124], "Stand by any yellow sign and press A. I\u2019ll take you anywhere in the city!": [1808.052, 4.212], "Later I\u2019ll teach you to read my canal map. When you see a ! over my head, come back. \u00a1Hasta luego!": [1812.714, 5.983], "Ahoy, {name}! I steer a water taxi now, with Pedro.": [1819.147, 2.975], "No more sneaking, just canals, boats and numbers. I love it!": [1822.571, 3.913], "Psst, {name}! Captain Jonah told me about his island fishing derby. Port Lumen has one too!": [1826.935, 5.321], "Catch two fish in the canals or the harbor, then tell me. We compare them. The longest goes on my board.": [1832.706, 6.196], "One derby a day. Ready, set, fish!": [1839.352, 2.484], "HELP WANTED. Board empty. Mayor Bea says: \"Notes soon! First learn to add and take away to 100 with Rafi.\"": [1842.286, 7.241], "HELP WANTED. You helped everyone today! New notes come every morning.": [1849.977, 4.169], "Tick-tock, {name}! I have two things for a number-line champion. What would you like?": [1854.597, 4.233], "Clock-hand jumps!. Learn to read a clock. Maybe later.": [1859.28, 3.337], "My big clock hands jump in tens! Want to help me count the jumps on a number line up to 100?": [1863.067, 5.94], "Yes, let\u2019s jump!. Maybe later.": [1869.457, 2.036], "Tick, tock, TEN! You jump in tens like a real clockmaker, {name}.": [1871.943, 3.849], "Can you keep a secret, {name}? Port Lumen has a magic creature!": [1876.243, 3.401], "On some nights, a little light glows in the Grand Canal. Look under the east bridge!": [1880.094, 4.852], "That is the Lanternhorse.": [1885.396, 1.631], "It only comes out at night, and only once in a while. See the glow? Cast your line right on it\u2026 be patient!": [1887.477, 6.324], "There is no hurry. It will still be there tomorrow night, or the next one.": [1894.251, 4.127], "Gus is right here, {name}. Say hello to him!": [1898.827, 2.484], "Then come and see me whenever you like. I'm in the Town Hall, up past the canal.": [1901.761, 4.553], "When the city is calm again, come and visit me! I'll be in the City Library, by the museums.": [1906.765, 5.343], "My hat shop is in the Galleria. Come and try on a hat when the clock is fixed!": [1912.557, 4.468], "Hello there! Say hello to our mayor first. She\u2019s right here!": [1917.475, 3.551], "Welcome to Port Lumen! I\u2019m Mayor Bea.": [1921.476, 2.484], "Since the storm, our big clock has stopped. Gus told me you came to help. Thank you, {name}!": [1924.41, 4.831], "Look at all the signs on Market Street! Some have words I bet you don\u2019t know yet. Shall we read them?": [1929.691, 5.641], "What a reader! Every sign on Market Street is clear now.": [1935.782, 3.209], "Oh no, oh no! My robot fell apart. Can you help me build something new with its pieces?": [1939.441, 5.407], "Beep boop! My new bridge works. Same pieces, new thing!": [1945.298, 3.359], "Ahoy, {name}! My harbor book needs a helper. What is moving in my harbor today?": [1949.107, 4.255], "My harbor book is shipshape. Fair winds, explorer!": [1953.811, 3.209]}}